course: dictionary
lesson: 7505
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and «pothole» is one of them. To choose the right meaning, read the words around it and ask: which meaning fits here?
explain: «Your local council ... fills potholes» and «a pothole is born» are about holes in a road. On a winter night water seeps into a tiny crack, freezes and pushes it wider, so the pothole is a hole in the surface of a road or path.
explain: The other meanings appear in different sentences. A pothole can also be a deep hole or cave in rock that people may climb down. Informally, it can mean a hidden problem that could cause trouble. Check the clues every time.
fact: A pothole is a hole in the surface of a road or path, made by weather and traffic.
fact: Potholes grow after winter because water gets into cracks, freezes, expands and breaks the road.
fact: A pothole can also be a deep hole or cave in rock, often made by water, that people may climb down.
fact: «Potholing» (UK) means exploring caves.
fact: Informally, a pothole is a hidden problem that could cause trouble.
exercise: «The council filled the pothole on our street.» What is a pothole here? | A deep cave where people climb down | *A hole in the surface of a road | A puddle after the rain | A hidden problem
exercise: Sam says, «The plan had a pothole that nobody saw until it was too late.» What does pothole mean here? | *A hidden problem that could cause trouble | A hole in the road | A cave full of bats | A bicycle wheel
exercise: «Some people go potholing in the hills.» What does potholing mean? | Counting bins | Fixing roads | *Exploring caves | Cycling through puddles
test: «Water seeps into a tiny crack, freezes and pushes it wider, and a pothole is born.» Where does the pothole form? | In the sky | *In the surface of a road | Inside a pen | On a book cover
test: «Tom explored a pothole in the hills, climbing down into the dark cave.» What does pothole mean here? | *A deep hole or cave in rock | A hidden problem | A bicycle wheel | A hole in a road
exam: Jayden says, «I hit a pothole on my bike.» What does pothole mean? | A deep cave in rock | *A hole in the surface of a road | A type of bin | A hidden problem that could cause trouble
